[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and marked known. Its reports hold three
problems, and each needs its own fix. Each has its own ticket, with the reports it covers, counted
the desk's way.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} filed={{ parser: 'https://github.com/preacherxp/support-kb-4471/issues/1', hint: 'https://github.com/preacherxp/support-kb-4471/issues/2', 'one-day move': 'https://github.com/preacherxp/support-kb-4471/issues/3' }} />

## The problems

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, so a tenant that writes the day
  first gets day and month swapped: a 7 April reminder goes out on 4 July. Any channel, any
  tenant on file. This is the fix #4471 was waiting for.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type the month
  first, as told, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. Only reports sent
  through the form of a booking-v3 tenant. The parser fix does not reach it: the hint has to match
  the tenant.
- **`one-day move`**: the date moves by one day, with no month swap. Tuesday 12 May shows as
  Monday 11 May; a client in Lisbon got Tuesday and one in Toronto got Monday. Neither the parser
  nor the hint explains that; it looks like a time zone shift. The desk read these apart
  (`desk-notes.json`), but the #4471 table still counts them under `parser`.

## Where they stand

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October.

- **`parser`**: fixed by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Ticket closed.
- **`hint`**: won't fix. The booking-v3 form is retired, so no new date comes in through its hint.
  Ticket closed as not planned.
- **`one-day move`**: open. Neither change moves a date back by one day.

## How the reports were split

- **One report per id.** The export pages overlap, so some reports appear twice in the file.
- **By tenant, not by intake tag.** Intake guesses from the reporter's browser. The cause depends
  on the tenant's locale, its booking form and the channel the report came in (`causes.ts`).
- **Not by subject.** The same subject turns up in more than one problem, and one problem comes in
  under many subjects.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but the <code>one-day move</code> is not fixed. Keep its ticket open until it is.
</Callout>

